# Referra Platform - Cursor AI Development Rules

> **CRITICAL**: This is a PRODUCTION application handling sensitive client data (HIPAA-adjacent).
> Security, data isolation, and code quality are NON-NEGOTIABLE.

## 🔖 Quick Reference for AI

**When citing rules, use these reference tags:**

**Security & Scripts:**
- `[CRITICAL: SECURITY-FIRST]` - Security requirements (non-negotiable)
- `[RULE: SCRIPTS-SECURITY]` - Never commit secrets in scripts
- `[PATTERN: SAFE-SCRIPT]` - Secure script template
- `[ANTI-PATTERN: UNSAFE-SCRIPT]` - Never do this in scripts
- `[RULE: GITIGNORE-SCRIPTS]` - Protecting risky scripts
- `[RULE: NO-CONSOLE-IN-PRODUCTION]` - Logging best practices

**Project Structure:**
- `[REFERENCE: SRC-ARCHITECTURE]` - Production-grade src/ organization
- `[REFERENCE: PROJECT-STRUCTURE]` - Root directory structure
- `[PATTERN: ROLE-BASED-PAGES]` - Adding new user role pages
- `[PATTERN: API-ROUTES]` - Organizing API routes by domain
- `[PATTERN: COMPONENTS]` - Organizing components by domain
- `[PATTERN: LIB-ORGANIZATION]` - Organizing business logic
- `[RULE: CONTINUOUS-BUILDING]` - Structure for future growth
- `[ANTI-PATTERN: AVOID-THESE]` - Bad organization patterns

**Code Patterns:**
- `[PATTERN: API-ROUTE]` - Standard API route implementation
- `[PATTERN: SERVER-ACTION]` - Server action pattern
- `[RULE: DATA-ISOLATION-REQUIRED]` - Organization data isolation requirements

**Code Philosophy:**
- `[PHILOSOPHY: NO-OVER-ENGINEERING]` - Production-grade WITHOUT fragmentation
- `[RULE: EXTRACT-WISELY]` - When to extract vs keep inline
- `[RULE: PERFORMANCE-CONSCIOUS]` - Fast, secure, cost-effective code

**Priority Order for Development:**
1. 🔒 **Security** - Authentication, authorization, data isolation, no secrets
2. ✅ **Functionality** - Feature works as specified
3. 🎨 **UX** - Loading, empty, error states
4. 📱 **Responsive** - Mobile-first design
5. ♿ **Accessible** - WCAG 2.1 AA compliance
6. 🧪 **Tested** - E2E tests passing

---

## Project Context

You are working on **Referra**, a multi-tenant referral management platform for social services organizations. This is a PRODUCTION application serving case managers, service providers, supervisors, and organization admins.

### Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 14+ (App Router, React Server Components)
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode)
- **Database**: MongoDB (native driver with custom connection pooling)
- **Auth**: NextAuth (with custom MongoDB adapter)
- **UI**: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui components
- **State**: React hooks, Server Actions for mutations
- **Testing**: Playwright for E2E tests
- **Deployment**: Vercel

### Core Business Context
- **Multi-tenant SaaS**: Strict organization-level data isolation
- **User Roles**: case_manager, provider, supervisor, org_admin
- **Core Workflow**: Case managers create referrals → Providers receive/respond → Status tracking
- **Compliance**: HIPAA-adjacent (handles sensitive client information)

---

## 🏗️ PRODUCTION-GRADE PROJECT STRUCTURE

### **[REFERENCE: SRC-ARCHITECTURE]** The `src/` Directory

**Core Principle**: Domain-driven organization with clear separation of concerns.

```
src/
├── app/                          # Next.js App Router (Pages & Layouts)
│   ├── (auth)/                  # Auth-protected route group
│   │   ├── case-manager/        # Case Manager role pages
│   │   ├── org-admin/           # Organization Admin role pages
│   │   ├── supervisor/          # Supervisor role pages
│   │   └── provider/            # Provider role pages (future)
│   ├── auth/                    # Authentication pages (public)
│   ├── invite/                  # Invitation/onboarding flow
│   ├── api/                     # API routes (organized by domain)
│   └── layout.tsx               # Root layout
│
├── components/                   # React components (organized by domain)
│   ├── [domain]/                # Domain-specific components
│   │   ├── [Component].tsx      # Main component files
│   │   ├── drawer/              # Drawer/modal components
│   │   └── hooks/               # Component-specific hooks
│   ├── layout/                  # Layout components (nav, sidebar)
│   ├── shared/                  # Shared/generic components
│   └── ui/                      # shadcn/ui base components
│
├── lib/                         # Business logic & utilities (organized by domain)
│   ├── [domain]/                # Domain-specific logic
│   │   ├── client.ts            # Client for API/DB calls
│   │   ├── actions.ts           # Server actions
│   │   ├── utils.ts             # Domain utilities
│   │   └── validation.ts        # Zod schemas
│   ├── mongodb/                 # MongoDB clients
│   │   ├── client.ts            # MongoDB connection
│   │   └── nextauth-adapter.ts  # NextAuth MongoDB adapter
│   ├── auth/                    # Authentication
│   │   ├── auth-minimal.ts      # NextAuth config
│   │   ├── helpers.ts           # Auth utilities
│   │   └── api-auth.ts          # API auth helpers
│   └── [utility].ts             # Shared utilities (email, etc.)
│
├── hooks/                       # Global React hooks
│   └── use-[feature].ts         # Custom hooks
│
├── types/                       # TypeScript type definitions
│   ├── [domain].ts              # Domain-specific types
│   └── index.ts                 # Shared types
│
├── contexts/                    # React Context providers
│   └── [Context]Provider.tsx
│
└── styles/                      # Global styles
    └── globals.css
```

