## 🔄 Git Workflow

### Commit Messages

**Use Conventional Commits:**
```bash
# Format: <type>(<scope>): <subject>

# Types:
feat:     # New feature
fix:      # Bug fix
refactor: # Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
style:    # Changes that don't affect code meaning (formatting, etc.)
docs:     # Documentation only changes
test:     # Adding or updating tests
chore:    # Changes to build process or auxiliary tools

# Examples:
git commit -m "feat(clients): add bulk import functionality" \
  -m "- Supports CSV file upload" \
  -m "- Validates data before import" \
  -m "- Shows progress indicator"

git commit -m "fix(referrals): resolve status update race condition" \
  -m "- Added optimistic locking" \
  -m "- Improved error handling"

git commit -m "refactor(auth): simplify session management"

git commit -m "docs: update API documentation for providers endpoint"
```

### Branch Naming

```bash
# Format: <type>/<ticket>-<description>

# Examples:
feature/REF-123-client-document-upload
fix/REF-456-referral-status-bug
refactor/REF-789-database-queries
chore/update-dependencies
```

### When to Commit

**Commit after each parent task completion:**
- All sub-tasks under parent task complete
- Tests passing
- No linter errors
- Code reviewed (if pair programming)

**Never commit:**
- Broken code
- Failing tests
- console.log() debugging statements
- Commented-out code
- .env files
- node_modules
- Temporary files

---

## 🚀 Deployment Checklist

Before deploying to production:

### Code Quality
- [ ] All tests passing
- [ ] No TypeScript errors
- [ ] No ESLint errors
- [ ] No console.log() statements
- [ ] Removed commented-out code
- [ ] Updated documentation

### Security
- [ ] Environment variables set in Vercel
- [ ] No secrets in code
- [ ] Data isolation tested (organizationId filtering)
- [ ] CORS configured correctly
- [ ] Rate limiting enabled

### Performance
- [ ] Database queries optimized
- [ ] Images optimized
- [ ] Bundle size acceptable
- [ ] Lighthouse score > 90

### Testing
- [ ] E2E tests passing
- [ ] Manual testing completed
- [ ] Mobile testing done
- [ ] Cross-browser testing done
- [ ] Load testing done (if high traffic expected)

### Monitoring
- [ ] Error tracking configured (Sentry)
- [ ] Analytics configured
- [ ] Logging configured
- [ ] Alerts configured

